.TH KAGI-VOLUME-IMAGE 1 "November 2026" "Kagi 0.39.0" "User Commands"
.SH NAME
kagi-volume-image \- copy a Kagi volume into a hypervisor image
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B scripts/kagi-volume-image
.I SOURCE OUTPUT
.BR qcow2 | vmdk | vhdx
.SH DESCRIPTION
Uses
.B qemu-img convert
to copy the raw contents of an NBD source into a new image file.
The accepted output formats are
.BR qcow2 ,
.BR vmdk ,
and
.BR vhdx .
Use a quiesced source if the export needs a consistent point-in-time view.
The exported image is an independent copy of the sparse Kagi volume.
.SH EXAMPLE
.nf
scripts/kagi-volume-image nbd://127.0.0.1:10809 vm.vhdx vhdx
.fi
.SH SEE ALSO
.BR kagi-volume-nbd (1),
.BR qemu-img (1)
